  "worked_solution": "Since $m\u2220A=m\u2220C={45}^{\u2218}$ and $AB=BC,$ we have an isosceles right triangle. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/218d08d1f46e608c5fb7d1c2f5ddd136e601e15514dc829c686b35ff42b15a8f.png)\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {9}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 81 \\\\  & =40.5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
